    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented for the owner soft-delete.\n\n## Change\n\n`DELETE /api/owners/{id}` now marks the owner deleted rather than removing the row, and the create-endpoint's duplicate/identity checks skip deleted owners.\n\n## Files touched (7)\n\n**Behavior:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`, as one self-contained block (default `false`, so a freshly created owner is not deleted).\n- `rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s the owner instead of `delete`ing it, so the row is retained and returns 2xx.\n- `rest/function/owner/EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique.java` \u2014 added `.filter(o -> !o.isDeleted())` so a soft-deleted owner no longer counts as an identity conflict.\n- `rest/function/owner/EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique.java` \u2014 same filter, so a deleted owner no longer blocks on the household (last-name + postcode) check.\n\n**Plumbing:**\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added `deleted` to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the flag and MapStruct maps it by name (surfaced on `GET`).\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column.\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 appended `FALSE` to the seed owner inserts (they're positional).\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n\nThe `deleted` field went onto the entity as a small, isolated field-plus-accessor block, and each of the three logic functions changed is the single method in its class (`WMC_other = 0`) with a one-line edit each. I deliberately kept the field off `BaseEntity`/`Person` (which would have forced schema changes across every entity table and coupled the concept to `Vet`), keeping the change cohesive to owners.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`. Both `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (new owner `deleted:false` \u2192 delete \u2192 still readable with `deleted:true`) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (recreating a deleted owner's duplicate is allowed) pass.",
